a few things RE FLOOR_RENDERING in render.cpp must be filled out; specifically, the
game must provide a ceiling/floor colour for each level, or a default if none was provided
this mostly depends on how levels are structured

sprites aren't being rendered on y = PIXELY-1
nor the sides of the screen x = 0 & x = PIXELX-1

add a timer library that lets you do stuff like
EVERY_MS(500) which is probably just a modulo under the hood

sprite.cpp requires the type Uint64 - a typedef defined by SDL
it's just uint64_t under the hood but...
sdl is only included in game.h 
embed the library into inc/thirdparty/ so the software ships with it

i want two different structures for textures: one for tiles & one for sprites
the sprites - animated or not - require a bit of extra information attached to each one
such as number of sprites, if it's a one-shot, etc; hence the need for the separate structure
each sprite will have a pointer to their currently attached texture and changing the sprite
will not happen often (for example, every frame) - unordered_map lookup time is not an issue
